WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:18.201
Morb was still in the dungeon, waiting for the trolls to arrive with the leeches.

2
00:00:18.202 --> 00:00:25.570
"So, Morb," Boz taunted, clutching the bars of his cell, "what happened to your prisoners at the zoo?

3
00:00:25.571 --> 00:00:31.613
My friend Teplo told me they all escaped. Now how could that have happened?"

4
00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:36.524
In the next cell, Teplo smirked. "Well, Boz, let me tell you.

5
00:00:36.525 --> 00:00:41.735
Apparently Morb's trolls were tricked by a pile of turnips."

6
00:00:41.736 --> 00:00:45.529
"Turnips, you say?" Boz laughed.

7
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:53.011
"That is correct," said Teplo. "Perhaps Morb's not as powerful as he thinks he is, huh?"

8
00:00:53.012 --> 00:01:02.880
Morb ignored the old men, his gaze moving past them to a couple huddled together in a cell farther down the corridor. He walked toward them.

9
00:01:02.881 --> 00:01:11.302
"Hello, Mother and Father," he greeted them with a twisted smile. "I hope the accommodations suit you."

10
00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.035
His mother looked up with tears in her eyes.

11
00:01:14.036 --> 00:01:17.610
"Why are you doing this, Morb?" she whispered.

12
00:01:17.611 --> 00:01:25.456
"Don't let him get to you, Mother!" a handsome young Red called from a few cells down. "He never did appreciate you."

13
00:01:25.457 --> 00:01:32.160
"True, I didn't appreciate being ignored and misunderstood," Morb snapped, glaring at his brother.

14
00:01:32.161 --> 00:01:34.880
Meanwhile his father climbed to his feet.

15
00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:39.138
"Son, please think about what you're doing," he said.

16
00:01:39.139 --> 00:01:42.325
"Didn't we teach you right from wrong?"

17
00:01:42.326 --> 00:01:52.355
Morb turned away from him. "You taught me that I'd better do whatever was necessary to take care of myself. And I learned that lesson well."

18
00:01:52.356 --> 00:02:00.390
"Nobody had to teach you to be selfish, Morb!" a young woman—one of his sisters—called from nearby. "You were born that way!"

19
00:02:00.391 --> 00:02:07.614
Morb ignored her too. He'd just heard heavy footsteps coming down the stairs. Good. The trolls were here.

20
00:02:07.615 --> 00:02:14.130
"Bring the cauldron to me," he called to them, not looking at his parents as his mother started to sob.

21
00:02:14.131 --> 00:02:19.487
"We'll start right here, in this cell."

22
00:02:19.488 --> 00:02:23.800
"I wish I had a map," Zann muttered, peeking around a corner.

23
00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:26.374
"I've got to get back to my friends."

24
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:31.198
Zann had been walking through the palace for some time and had not yet found an exit.

25
00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:35.949
All he'd found were winding stairways and dark, narrow corridors.

26
00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.150
The palace was much bigger than he'd realized.

27
00:02:39.151 --> 00:02:44.901
Creeping down another flight of steps, Zann diligently watched for any trolls that might be around.

28
00:02:44.902 --> 00:02:47.728
He thought briefly about just zapping out.

29
00:02:47.729 --> 00:02:51.833
After all, that Deceleration spell hadn't attracted Morb's attention.

30
00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:55.907
But it probably wasn't worth the risk. There had to be a way out somewhere.

31
00:02:55.908 --> 00:03:03.101
"Aha!" Zann whispered when he saw sunlight pouring in through a large doorway at the end of a long hallway.

32
00:03:03.102 --> 00:03:10.983
He hurried forward. But the doorway was not an exit—it led to a balcony overlooking the huge courtyard at the center of the palace.

33
00:03:10.984 --> 00:03:19.139
"What in the world is that?" Zann blurted out in surprise when he saw the huge, dark, hulking shape in the middle of the courtyard.

34
00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.802
Zann immediately thought about what Gliss had told them yesterday.

35
00:03:22.803 --> 00:03:29.253
Could this be the horrible magic-sucking machine that Morb had built to help him take over Magica?

36
00:03:29.254 --> 00:03:34.353
He was still staring at the machine when he heard voices approaching. One of them belonged to Slib.

37
00:03:34.354 --> 00:03:38.353
"Uh-oh," Zann whispered. There was nowhere to hide on the balcony.

38
00:03:38.354 --> 00:03:42.997
Looking around, Zann saw some pebbles in a planter. They gave him an idea.

39
00:03:42.998 --> 00:03:47.661
He picked up one of the pebbles and threw it down the hall, past Slib and the others.

40
00:03:47.662 --> 00:03:50.641
It hit a wall and made a sound. Click!

41
00:03:50.642 --> 00:03:57.943
"What was that?" said Slib. Everyone turned around, and Zann quickly dashed into a room across the hall.

42
00:03:57.944 --> 00:04:03.758
"I'm sure it's nothing," said someone else, as the group continued walking closer to Zann.

43
00:04:03.759 --> 00:04:08.947
Zann held his breath—he could hear Slib and the others right outside the door.

44
00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:16.924
"You can believe what I say since I'm now Morb's most trusted adviser," Slib was bragging.

45
00:04:16.925 --> 00:04:21.358
"The era of Reds is truly over, just as I predicted.

46
00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:27.592
Thanks to King Morb, the rest of us will now have the power we deserve."

47
00:04:27.593 --> 00:04:31.898
One of his companions murmured something in response, but Zann wasn't listening.

48
00:04:31.899 --> 00:04:37.516
He barely had time to dash through another doorway before Slib and the others came into the room.

49
00:04:37.517 --> 00:04:41.742
Zann found himself in a hallway lined with half a dozen doors.

50
00:04:41.743 --> 00:04:45.527
Behind him, he could hear Slib still bragging loudly.

51
00:04:45.528 --> 00:04:47.543
Zann reached for the first door.

52
00:04:47.544 --> 00:04:51.388
"Ouch!" he blurted out, as the doorknob burned his hand.

53
00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:58.820
"Did you hear that?" Slib's muffled voice came from the other room. "There's someone behind that door."

54
00:04:58.821 --> 00:05:01.501
Zann gulped. He had to get out of sight!

55
00:05:01.502 --> 00:05:07.000
But when he looked down the hall, all the doorknobs were glowing red, just like the one he'd touched.

56
00:05:07.001 --> 00:05:12.707
No—not all of them. He spotted one doorknob that was glowing blue.

57
00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:15.327
He hurried toward it, but then he hesitated.

58
00:05:15.328 --> 00:05:18.422
Who had put a spell on these doors, and why?

59
00:05:18.423 --> 00:05:20.955
He'd never seen this kind of spell before.

60
00:05:20.956 --> 00:05:26.286
Normally people just used an ordinary Shield spell if they wanted to keep others out of a room.

61
00:05:26.287 --> 00:05:29.333
Then he heard the door behind him start to open.

62
00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:32.991
If he didn't get out of this hallway, Slib would see him!

63
00:05:32.992 --> 00:05:37.518
Grabbing the blue doorknob, he was relieved to find it cool under his hand.

64
00:05:37.519 --> 00:05:41.295
He pushed through the door, allowing it to fall shut behind him.

65
00:05:41.296 --> 00:05:45.977
He found himself in what appeared to be a dusty old storage room.

66
00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:49.329
The only light came through a single barred window.

67
00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:55.328
Boxes and crates were piled everywhere, and a couple of dust bugs scuttled off behind a trunk.

68
00:05:55.329 --> 00:05:59.875
Zann heard a sound behind him. Spinning around, he gasped.

69
00:05:59.876 --> 00:06:09.998
Standing in a dim corner of the room was the old woman he and his friends had met in Wormwood.
